# 6. Project Testing

## Project Title

EduGenie: Google Gemini Powered Learning Assistant

## Testing Objective

The objective of testing is to verify that all major EduGenie functionalities work correctly and that the application handles user inputs properly.

## Test Cases

| Test Case ID | Functionality | Input | Expected Result |
|---|---|---|---|
| TC01 | Question Answering | What is photosynthesis? | Relevant educational answer |
| TC02 | Concept Explanation | Explain gravity simply | Simple explanation |
| TC03 | Quiz Generation | Pythagoras Theorem | Quiz questions are generated |
| TC04 | Summarization | Educational paragraph | Concise summary |
| TC05 | Learning Recommendation | Learn Python | Useful learning suggestions |
| TC06 | Learning Path | SQL | Structured learning path |
| TC07 | Empty Input | Blank request | Validation message |
| TC08 | Invalid Input | Invalid request | Appropriate error message |
| TC09 | API Error | Gemini unavailable | Error handling message |
| TC10 | Frontend | User request | Correct response displayed |

## Functional Testing

The following functionalities are tested:

- User input
- Question answering
- Concept explanation
- Quiz generation
- Summarization
- Learning recommendations
- Learning path generation
- API communication

## Performance Testing

The application should provide responses within a reasonable time under normal internet and API conditions.

## Security Testing

The following security checks are performed:

- API keys are not exposed.
- User input is validated.
- Sensitive information is not stored in public files.

## Expected Testing Result

All major functionalities should work correctly and provide useful educational responses.

## Conclusion

Testing helps ensure that EduGenie is reliable, usable, and ready for demonstration.
